  "methods": [
    "Export historical throughput variation; never run a benchmark.\n\nreport.rep stores operations in nominal one-second reporter intervals, with\nrounded elapsed seconds. Its elapsed origin is reporter launch, not process\nlaunch; process UTC timestamps are recorded separately without false alignment.\n",
    "60 s is a descriptive common cutoff for the initial ramp, not a replacement for the original 300 s measurement.",
    "C r02 and f06 report 299 complete intervals; the unreported final fraction is not invented.",
    "Different workloads are not mixed into hourly averages; actual process UTC spans are retained.",
    "A persistent outside workload could produce a stable slowdown. Smooth throughput does not rule it out."
